    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2829" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anthrax</span></b> , ăcis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθραξ</span> (coal). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Natural cinnabar</i> (the color of which is like a
			burning coal), <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7, 8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In medic., <i>a virulent
				ulcer</i> (in pure Lat., carbunculus), Aem. Macr. de Herb. c.
			de Sabina.</div>
